Chapter 10-35: "The White Sheep"

Subaru's head hits the floor with a heavy thud.

Seeing that head fall without any restraint, I instinctively thought—*This is bad.*

――――

I've seen wounds and blood more times than I care to count, both at the healing clinic and on battlefields I was dispatched to for missions. So I understand. People who've taken truly grave wounds can't even manage to protect themselves.

Just like Subaru now, unable to even guard his head as he collapses to the floor.

――――

Slowly, blood seeps from Subaru's right side and flows, soaking the landing. Whenever I see blood, I always think—*It's as if life itself is draining away.*

"Hey, isn't it somehow so mysterious? Red and white are such a wonderfully matching combination, and every time I see it I'm utterly captivated... but right now, more than that—you! You, why did you do such a thing? Could it be... jealousy? And that means... love!?"

Whether that was truly her impression of the same scene is doubtful, but after commenting on the blood flowing from the collapsed Subaru and the whiteness of the floor, Lycoris turns both her hands toward her—toward "The White Sheep."

Having stabbed Subaru from behind, "The White Sheep" wore a terribly cold expression. Wiping her blood-stained fingers with a handkerchief, she quietly stared back at Lycoris, and then—

――――!

"Yes, it's love. In the end, all our motivations come down to that, don't they?"

"Affirmation!? So that means it really is that! Natsuki is head over heels for Felix, and you couldn't bear it so you stabbed him! What a tragedy! You, driven mad by jealousy, and Felix, crying out as he faces love head-on... which one should I root for!?"

The temperature difference between "The White Sheep" and Lycoris's responses is staggering. But Felix, who favors neither, was internally angered by the absurdity of Lycoris's words.

To say Felix is crying out—there's a limit to how distorted one's view can be.

He's not crying out. He's just—

"—Subaru-kun! No! Don't die! Come here... let him come here!"

—He's just, as a healer worth his salt, calling out to someone dying.

"What a tragedy."

Shaking his body, putting strength into his arms, he struggles desperately to reach Subaru. But Felix's body, pinned against the wall, won't budge an inch.

Meanwhile, Lycoris advances to the center of the landing with the sound of her footsteps. Right between Felix and "The White Sheep"—there, she extends both hands toward the two of them.

"On one side, the one you chased after, overcoming even the 'Detour' with blood-spitting determination. On the other side, the one who could only cling to that desperate back from the closest place. And such a sinful Natsuki will pass away, leaving you two behind... this is it!"

"—This is, what exactly?"

"Love burns brighter the higher the obstacles, right? Age and gender are also kindling to stoke love. But then, what's the greatest obstacle? It's *se-pa-ra-tion*!"

――――

"Death! That's love's greatest obstacle! Because when you die, it's over! You can never touch the one who's died again. So nothing keeps two people apart more than death, right? Conversely, death is the medicine that raises the love between two people who love each other to its extreme! Death is an aphrodisiac!"

She's insane. Lycoris, speaking with an ecstatic smile and eyes, was out of her mind.

How much "The White Sheep" agreed with that deranged love theory, I don't know. But she neither laughed at nor disparaged Lycoris's ravings—

"—Mama, thank you as always. I love you more than anyone in the world."

It was a statement with no context whatsoever, sudden, and moreover, incomprehensible.

At least to Felix, it seemed—like Subaru before he was stabbed—to be caused by "The White Sheep"'s mental imbalance brought on by the "poison" Lycoris was scattering.

But—

――――

To Lycoris, whose blood drained in an instant and whose face went pale, it struck her completely differently.

At Lycoris's state, a change came over "The White Sheep"'s cold expression. A smile. She wore a cold sneer ill-suited to her features—

"—I am an 'Beloved Child' sent to the 'Six-Tongued' by Mama."

"—Ah."

"I infiltrated to grasp the full picture of the 'Six-Tongued' and expose the enemy completely. But at this rate, it seemed like 'Beloved Children' would end up clashing with each other, so I revealed myself. —Please think of this as a souvenir. She was quite a formidable person, you know. If she'd been acting normally."

Saying "this," she kicked Subaru's body lying in the pool of blood with her toe. At "The White Sheep"'s rough treatment, the frozen Lycoris exhaled slowly, deeply.

It wasn't the sigh of a woman seeing nightmares, but one of deep, deep relief.

"Ah, ah, so that's it. You're also a 'Beloved Child'... you're not Mama herself, right? Then that's good. You see, Mama does that sometimes, doesn't she? To truly understand each other's feelings, I once had a day where everyone I met was Mama! When I remembered that, I thought my heart would freeze. ...You're not Mama, right?"

"Yes, I am myself. But I understand the feeling. I've also been subjected to things that made food unable to pass down my throat, many times."

"You too! We're the same... is that why you confided in me? Does that mean it's fate? You don't want to lose me? Me too!"

At the feet of the two "Beloved Children" chatting amicably, the blood of the boy pathetically abandoned by love continues to flow, bit by bit, but surely, shaving away his life. With each second, the possibility of picking up that spilling life is lost.

"And yet, what are you taking your time for, you two... I also...!"

Hateful. Infuriating. Frustrating. These "Beloved Children" who prepared this blood hourglass, and myself who can only watch without doing anything—and moreover, Subaru who blundered in here and got himself neatly stabbed by the traitor—my anger is immense.

These past two months, it's been like this the whole time. I've been unbearably angry at Subaru, constantly.

—Why did Subaru leave Emilia's side?

Why is he once again leaving the person who should be closest to him, trying to extend a hand to Crusch's predicament? Because of that, he's separated from his lord and comrades, and now he's in a pool of blood. It's completely backwards.

Natsuki Subaru's actions, his very existence, are Felix Argyle's sin itself.

If he was robbed because of weakness, and can only seek compensation for that fate from those around him, then having Subaru make up for it—all of it is Felix's sin. —And moreover, Felix's sins always end up being paid not by himself, but by someone other than himself.

"Don't be ridiculous..."

Once, Felix's birth destroyed the Argyle family—because the beast-ear trait appearing as an atavism of demi-human blood made his father suspect his mother's infidelity.

Once, Felix's arrogance made him miss the chance to repay his teacher. —His greatly indebted teacher who affirmed this power was doubted for that judgment, and was killed by someone who'd reached their limit.

Once, Felix's negligence meant he couldn't save the best friend he truly respected and loved. —While being celebrated as "Blue," with power unbefitting that fame, he let his lord's beloved slip away.

Once, Felix's atonement never reached his lord, more important than life itself, twice over. —And even now, his own inadequacy was about to cause a third betrayal of his lord.

"That's just... not funny... it's not funny at all...!"

He twists his body. His arms won't come free. He puts strength into his shoulders. His arms won't tear off. He kicks the wall with all his might. His arms won't become free. Nothing goes as he wishes. Just like Felix's life.

"—"

Anger with no direction runs wild inside his hatefully thin chest. He can maintain his body's completeness, but he can't maintain his heart's. Rather, has there ever been a time when his heart was complete? Always emotionally unstable, his fragile heart making a ruckus.

That's why, like always, not a single person—

"—Ah."

Again, he'll be punished. By ruining someone else's life. —Cursing the fate entwined with Felix's life, he gritted his teeth—when it happened.

――――

His eyes met Subaru's black eyes, lying in the pool of blood with his face turned sideways.

Limbs sprawled limply, pupils unfocused, repeating thin breaths mixed with blood bubbles—that face was unmistakably that of a person on the verge of death, something Felix had seen many times.

Just one thing. The difference from those trapped by death and being called away—there's just one difference.

Those being called away die with grief, fear, and regret in their eyes. But Subaru was different. In his powerless, blurred black eyes resided hope.

—The moment he understood what that hope was directed at, Felix comprehended.

The terrifyingly foolish reliance on others that the weak, fragile, powerless Natsuki Subaru had enacted.

"Don't be ridiculous...!"

What spilled out next was different from the directionless anger of before. It was directed straight at the one it should be directed at—a crystallization of the curse-like anger swirling thickly within Felix.

At this late stage, Natsuki Subaru believes in Felix Argyle. —This is an absurdly stupid one-man show performed with only that hope as its basis.

