—That was before Subaru and "The White Sheep" went underground.

"I'll choose too. —So that I can face that person with my head held high."

Accepting "The White Sheep"'s decision, Subaru determined their course: underground.

While avoiding the safety-first approach of slamming the brakes, he doesn't intend to equate that with recklessness. Relying on "Cor Leonis" to probe Ferris's location while leaving route correction to "The White Sheep"'s instructions, without rushing but at the highest speed they could muster, the two approached their destination.

But simply arriving at the destination without any means would be meaningless.

"Hey, isn't it weird? Why is the enemy keeping Ferris alive?"

While concentrating his consciousness on his Authority during the journey, Subaru also focused on increasing his hand of cards.

In many cases, usable cards sleep among the trash cards. And even without deliberately trying to collect them, trash cards are buried in large quantities in time spent casually.

This isn't limited to since visiting this castle. It's also within these past two months of groping in the dark.

"Following Capella's policy of not killing as much as possible... would be rejected because my own life is pitiful, so setting that aside, I can think of two patterns."

One: Ferris's healing ability far exceeds the enemy's imagination, and actually the opponent thought they'd dealt the finishing blow, leaving his near-death body abandoned underground.

And the other—

"—The pattern where the enemy has a reason to keep Ferris alive."

"You mean they want information, or to use him as a hostage...?"

"That's the most likely story. But considering my pitiful experience points, I can think of one extremely unpleasant reason. —The line that Capella wants to adopt Ferris too."

When told that "Beloved Children" are gathered for their specialized talents, Subaru felt Ferris would be perfect for it. Of course, trying to analyze Capella's twisted love is a reckless endeavor, so it's only speculation based on the current situation.

"...That might be possible. No, it might be the most convincing story."

"If 'White Sheep'-chan also thinks it's likely, that's reassuring. Honestly, I thought it was a shitty idea... and then I realized I did the same thing, taking in someone I captured, and I was shocked."

"Eh? Eh? Ehhh?"

"The White Sheep" was astonished at Subaru reflecting on himself, but detailed explanations are noise, so he skips them.

Needless to say, it's about Meili, but he wants to assert there's a decisive difference in educational philosophy from Capella. —There are also other things he wants to discuss with Meili about this matter, but that's for later.

"Anyway, if this possibility holds, oddly enough, we might not need to worry about Ferris being killed. But even in that case, I still recommend rendezvousing with Ferris."

"...Can I ask your reasons?"

"There are two. One is the same as before we started running: with Ferris, survival rates are dramatically different. The second is the enemy's ability problem. I want to do something about the most dangerous one, 'Lost Child.'"

Nodding at "The White Sheep," who took a small breath, Subaru advances his feet while tracing the wall with his hand.

Currently, of the "Beloved Children" who appeared in the Kugelsschreiber Castle, the known ones are three: "Silence," "Collapse," and "Lost Child," but Subaru considers the last one the most formidable. Of course, "Silence"'s assassin capabilities and "Collapse"'s troublesome nature go without saying.

"If we can fight now, Crusch-san has countermeasures against 'Silence.' And for 'Collapse,' I have a method in mind. But 'Lost Child' is different. As long as this exists, we can never rendezvous with our allies."

The reason Subaru can currently attempt to rendezvous with Ferris is because two conditions are cleared: the effect of "Cor Leonis" and Ferris not moving from that spot. The most terrifying thing about "Lost Child" is that the moment the target starts moving, the difficulty of rendezvous skyrockets.

"So I have to get 'Lost Child' lifted. For that, Ferris's..."

"W-wait, I'm being left behind! That emotion-panic ability, can you really do something about it!?"

"Yeah, I think I can. Can't say 100%, and it pisses me off to rely on that bastard Regulus's power, but I've confirmed that the Authority ranks above 'Lost Child.'"

Feeling "The White Sheep" staring at him intently, having lost her voice, Subaru opens his eyelids. While deliberating, Ferris's location is now before them; he needs to discuss this here.

Because this strategy Subaru thought of absolutely requires "The White Sheep"'s cooperation.

"—'White Sheep'-chan, I have a plan I want you to hear. It's a strategy that depends on you whether it's doable, so I want your opinion."

"A strategy? And it depends on me..."

"As you know, if there are enemies ahead, it's quite doubtful whether the two of us can handle them head-on. So here, I want to be cunning and set up a surprise attack."

"A surprise attack..." "The White Sheep," having stopped alongside Subaru who uttered those words, prompts him to continue.

"Please tell me. What do you want me to do?"

"Straight to it: 'White Sheep'-chan is a spy sent by Capella into the 'Six-Tongued.' Then, you capture me, who was secretly trying to counterattack, and rejoin the 'Beloved Children'... something like that."

"—! That's..."

"I said it, right? 'Beloved Children' barely know each other. But 'White Sheep'-chan actually has a past as a 'Beloved Child,' so you have common topics with them. If you had me as a souvenir, wouldn't it seem more promising than a head-on fight?"

It must have been quite unexpected. "The White Sheep" covered her mouth with both hands, eyes wide open. Of course, it's not as easy as it sounds, and the opponent won't just naively believe it.

But in these two months of the "Beloved Children" front, Subaru has seen many times how the enemy shares less information than expected, fighting to answer Capella within the scope of their given functions and authority.

The dictatorship of Capella at the top, the deliberate lack of coordination among allies for discipline purposes, and the false loyalty bound by fear—Subaru bets there's room to exploit.

However, this requires "The White Sheep" herself to have the resolve to face that fear again.

"I think... there's a chance. Perhaps, for reasons 'Ash Star'-san doesn't know, it might work even better than expected."

"Seriously? I'm curious about the reason you don't know, but if it's a plus, it's more than welcome."

"But we might stumble at the first step. Even if you bring 'Ash Star'-san, whether they'll trust you for it..."

"—Then how about this: what if we prepare a situation where they have no choice but to believe?"

The anticipated objection from "The White Sheep"—Subaru agrees. Even if "The White Sheep" brought Subaru with his hands tied behind his back, there's a high chance they'd see through it as a desperate gamble.

So the proposal was prepared in two stages. However, it's a plan with a heavy burden on "The White Sheep."

Because—

"...'White Sheep'-chan, do you have any weapons?"

"Weapons...? A collapsible staff for staff techniques, and, well, a short blade. Will you use them?"

"Yeah, I'll have you use them. ...For impact, the knife, right..."

Shown the two types of weapons concealed on her—a staff about the length of a baton and a short blade shaped like a survival knife—Subaru considers the latter suitable for the purpose.

And to "The White Sheep," confused by his grim expression, he declared:

"—When we run into a 'Beloved Child,' stab me with that knife. If you go that far, surely it'll add considerable persuasiveness, don't you think?"

