"If persuasiveness is lacking, add persuasiveness. I also considered the pattern of beating me half to death, but that won't fool Todd. I mean, he's cautious and suspicious."

――――

"Estimating the enemy generously and doing something half-hearted won't draw results. If we're doing this, it's all-in, full force."

"W-wait..."

"I'll also give the performance of a lifetime, a truly convincing act of being done in. But the burden is definitely greater on 'White Sheep'-chan, so whether you can do it—"

"—Wait, please!"

His mouth, rapidly explaining the strategy overview, was silenced by that shout.

Having raised her voice, "The White Sheep" placed the hand that had been covering her mouth on her own chest, checking its beat with her palm, turning tear-moistened eyes toward Subaru. —As expected, it was too unreasonable.

He knew from the start that "The White Sheep" was a gentle soul who disliked conflict. Even if it's a strategy, asking her to stab Subaru is just too cruel—

"...That's not your true intention, Subaru-san."

"...'White Sheep'-chan?"

"That, putting yourself in danger to increase the chance I'll succeed—that's not your true intention. ...I made you say it."

Tightly gripping the chest of her clothes, "The White Sheep" shrinks her thin shoulders, her voice trembling.

But Subaru doesn't understand the meaning of her words. Even if told he made her say it, he has no recollection. The one who thought of this plan was unmistakably Subaru.

Still, to calm her, who's growing weak and small, he reaches a hand toward her shoulder—

"I don't really understand what you're saying. Maybe you're confused from the shock—"

"—! Don't touch me!"

"—!" His hand, about to touch her, was brushed away, and Subaru involuntarily gasped. For a moment, "The White Sheep" also stiffened her cheeks at her own overreaction, but she quickly pressed her lips together—

"Please don't touch me. If you touch me, surely, Subaru-san will become more..."

"More? More what. 'White Sheep'-chan, I don't get it. We don't have time to dawdle right now. Please, just say it clearly!"

"I'll become more obedient to me! That's my power!"

To Subaru, who raised his voice, "The White Sheep" raised her voice even more, showing her own two hands. Her left and right hands with slender, supple fingers—showing them clearly to Subaru—

"My power is 'Coaxer'... the power to make people I touch with these hands develop affection for me. People who develop affection for me can't refuse my requests..."

"'White Sheep'-chan's... requests..."

"Don't you have any recollection? When I held your hand and talked to you, somehow you felt what I was saying was right, and you agreed..."

Being told that, Subaru closes his eyes and recalls the two months since meeting "The White Sheep."

Certainly, there may have been such scenes several times. When troubled by decisions or lost, being touched by "The White Sheep" and going along with the proposal she voiced—several times.

"But that's..."

"—I don't like this power. I hate it. Because I think I'm trampling on everyone there, using them for my own sake."

――――

"So, normally, I tried to stay away from Subaru-san and Beatrice-san as much as possible. Being careful not to accidentally touch you..."

That admirable effort is probably true. She avoided physical contact with others as much as she could. And yet, on the rare occasions when she did hold Subaru's hand—

"Russell-san's instruction, huh. Not just that 'White Sheep'-chan was a former 'Beloved Child,' but with that power too, she was extremely valued. Now that you mention it, it makes sense."

No wonder that Russell counted "The White Sheep," who was clearly personality-wise unsuited, as one of the main forces against the "Six-Tongued." In a sense, she's a practitioner of honey traps with an outstanding success rate, requiring no seduction.

"So the current plan is also the result of me being coaxed by 'White Sheep'-chan."

"—. Yes."

Nodding solemnly, "The White Sheep" looks like a sinner who has repented and confessed her crime.

In fact, that's probably how it is emotionally for her. Drawing out others' affection with an innate power, inviting results convenient for herself. She's tormented by the awareness of having committed every vice.

And now, with Subaru proposing a plan to injure himself, the guilt she'd been carrying exploded. The influence of "Collapse" making emotions uncontrollable is probably also significant.

Then, surely Subaru is also affected by "Collapse." —Otherwise, he would never say such a thing to "The White Sheep."

"'White Sheep'-chan."

"I'm sorry, but please reconsider. That, that reckless plan is no good. A plan where I'm safe but you might die..."

"—I have someone I really, really like, so I won't die for 'White Sheep'-chan's sake."

"—. ——. ————Eh."

At Subaru's confession, "The White Sheep," who'd worn a sinner's face, was dumbfounded, eyes wide. And sorry to her, who can't argue back, but time is precious. He continues while she's stunned.

He has to correct "The White Sheep"'s misunderstanding.

"Sure, 'White Sheep'-chan is quite the beautiful girl, but in my heart, that person is the first star... her brilliance looks different. So I'm not being coaxed by you."

――――

"And, one more misunderstanding... or rather, this is my bad explanation, but I said whether this plan is doable depends on 'White Sheep'-chan, right. But what I'm counting on in this plan isn't 'White Sheep'-chan."

"Th-then, who...?"

Subaru sincerely regrets causing "The White Sheep" unnecessary worry. He did her wrong. —From the start, the risk premises were different for Subaru and "The White Sheep."

"The White Sheep" thought this plan carried the risk that Subaru might die.

But Subaru is different. This plan might cause Subaru pain enough to wish he were dead, but it's a plan where he won't die.

Because—

"—It's Ferris. I'm counting on him."

"Ah..."

"He said it. In front of him, even someone who wants to die won't be allowed to die. So this plan only works in front of him."

In exchange, if it happens in front of Ferris, he'll uphold his verbal promise on his pride.

For if something happens to Beatrice, in just two months, he'd rewrite the principles of healing magic to save even spirits. Because there's respect for that gentle strength of his.

He asks Ferris for the same reliance on others as he does Reinhard and Julius. —That is the core of this "Natsuki Subaru Fake Murder Case."

"Also, I just said I'm not being coaxed, but I think we have become friendly. But that's not just because of your power—you talk to me when I'm struggling, you take the initiative to make tea during breaks, and also because I'm easy."

"Subaru-san..."

"I don't think I was tricked by you. Let's help each other as comrades. Compared to me suddenly being stabbed in front of Ferris, isn't this a much better proposal?"

Saying that, Subaru deliberately extends his right hand, inviting "The White Sheep" to shake. Looking down at the offered hand, "The White Sheep" takes a deep breath.

"...I can't believe in people's kindness. Even your words now, Subaru-san, I end up thinking maybe my power made you say them. That's why I couldn't with that person either."

――――

"But... but, today, I'll try believing. That you, who says you can believe in someone other than me, more than me—"

Hesitantly, the extending hand touches Subaru's, and it's firmly grasped. The exchanged handshake is proof that she, who feared manipulating the hearts of those she touched, took a step of courage.

And the use of that courage she stepped forward with—is to stab Subaru.

"What a conclusion, but can you do it? 'White Sheep'-chan."

"Melty."

"Eh?"

"—Melty Pristis. That's my name."

To Subaru, eyes round, "The White Sheep"—no, Melty Pristis, loosens her lips.

It's the face of a girl who, while harboring cowardice in her heart, decided to resist with mustered courage. Surprising Subaru with such a smile and self-introduction, she puts strength into their shaking hands—

"This is my first time making a friend, and my first time stabbing a friend!"

It was, indeed, a brave friend's declaration.

Accepting it, the "Natsuki Subaru Fake Murder Case" was set to be executed—

